WEBVTT

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.440
What are you drawing?

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:29.000
March of the Behemoth

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.610
Is this your first time on a train?

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.970
Huh? W-Well...

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:57.040
My father told me about them,
 but this is my first time riding one.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.100
Are you traveling alone?

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:11.220
Oh... No.

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:17.830
You'll be able to see it soon.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.890
It measures 219 meters long.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:31.320
It's the largest in the continent.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:36.230
This area acts as a border between 
the north and the south.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:41.270
It's said that this iron bridge, constructed
 after the war, is a bridge of peace that

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:44.190
connects the north and the south.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.850
Wow, it's so amazing!

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:47.910
We have to tell Daddy all about it!

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.440
Of course. Once we get to the other side.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.900
In addition to carrying people and cargo,

00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:00.920
this iron bridge supports the everyday 
lives of the people living in peace.

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:04.550
That tragic war is now over.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:09.420
From now on, the people and the iron bridge
 will be moving forward into the future.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.010
The war's over now!

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:19.770
But it's not over... None of it.

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:23.430
None of us were able to finish it.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:28.820
Fire!

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:55.460
What's going on?

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:56.970
Well, uh...

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:06.530
Wh-What? What's going on?

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:12.010
Liza?

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.730
I need you to come with me at once.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:20.120
The Incarnate Behemoth is moving 
much faster than expected.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.610
We're currently here.

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:34.210
Our target is currently five kilometers 
to our west, and on the move.

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:39.840
Ever since we discovered Behemoth, 
it's been moving east.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:44.360
If that was all, we wouldn't 
be in our current predicament.

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.260
The problem is...

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:48.140
The iron bridge?

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:48.830
Yes.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:53.750
If it continues, it's certain to 
crash into the iron bridge.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:58.990
We have to stop it from destroying 
the iron bridge at all costs.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:07.520
This iron bridge supports the everyday 
lives of the people living in peace.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:13.060
We tried to stop it,

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:15.310
but our strength was not enough...

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:18.230
If only we knew its motive...

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:21.260
Do you have any ideas?

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:27.120
Well?

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.000
No.

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:34.480
Even cannons have no effect 
against Behemoth's giant body.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:40.180
On top of that, anywhere he is injured will 
regrow and become even more reinforced.

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:43.740
The more we wound him,
 the harder he'll be to deal with.

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:47.820
It's impossible to fatally wound him
 with your current equipment.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:52.160
But... there is a way.

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:01.740
He's coming.

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:33.170
Don't falter! Follow the plan!

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:39.320
Fire!

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:48.290
Don't stop firing! Fire! Fire!

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:57.420
Because of all the wounds 
he sustained during the war,

00:07:57.420 --> 00:08:01.100
his whole body has hardened so much 
that it can deflect cannonballs.

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:01.880
However...

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:05.590
<i>The backs of his joints,
which were protected from attacks...</i>

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:09.840
<i>Got him.</i>

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:30.730
Huh? Wait... Is that true?

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:33.250
Yes. That's what the report says.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:59.870
He hasn't hurt anyone?

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:00.900
Correct.

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:04.980
Behemoth has been avoiding populated cities 
and towns the whole time he's been moving.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.850
Because of that, there haven't 
been any casualties reported.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:11.210
Even the soldiers who were injured

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:15.650
weren't hurt by direct attacks from Behemoth.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:17.110
That means he...

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:21.040
He still has some of his 
humanity left, most likely.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:28.880
U-Um...

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:38.390
My name is Schaal.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:41.510
My father was John William Bancroft.

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:43.890
He's an Incarnate, just like you.

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:52.110
Why are you heading east?

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:58.010
Please... Is there any way I 
can convince you to turn back?

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:01.500
There's a very important 
iron bridge up ahead.

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:08.030
If you turn back, I'm sure the military 
won't bother you anymore, either.

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:18.540
As I thought... There must 
be something up ahead.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:28.900
Right over there.

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:32.860
Why haven't you killed it yet?!

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:37.760
That Beast is still alive! Why didn't 
you finish it off immediately?!

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:40.790
Again, we have protocol that we have to follo—

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:44.020
Protocol? What are you babbling about?

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:48.500
How do you plan on taking responsibility if 
that thing harms my precious iron bridge?

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:50.870
This is all to protect the iron bridge.

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:56.320
Behemoth has a giant body and
a troublesome healing ability.

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:58.890
It would be difficult to 
dispose of him right now.

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:04.140
So our plan is to cause an explosion on the 
cliff before the iron bridge and fill the valley.

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:07.720
We'll cut off his route and, after we've 
secured the safety of the iron bridge,

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:09.640
we plan to take care of Behemoth.

00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:14.990
If you have enough explosives to fill the valley,
 why don't you use them on the monster?!

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:16.400
It's just a stupid beast!

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:19.860
If you set off dynamite on it, 
it'll be blown to smithereens!

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:25.160
If you military folk can't handle it,
 we'll just do it ourselves!

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:26.990
We know how to use explosives!

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:28.950
We won't be changing our plan.

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:32.750
We're done with them!

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:37.140
Those pathetic losers didn't even try! 
It's no use talking to them!

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:41.920
Are all railway presidents like that?

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:43.460
Good grief.

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:46.190
Please get to work.

00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:47.080
Yes, sir!

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:55.140
The work is going well.

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:59.190
The explosives will be set by the 
end of tomorrow, as scheduled.

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:02.140
Could you set some at this point, too?

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:05.330
Huh? B-But that's...

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:07.080
Just in case.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:09.270
You can do it after you're done here.

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:10.830
Understood, sir.

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:17.400
Do you have a moment?

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:22.100
So, what did you want to ask?

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:23.810
About him.

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:28.880
Artie... Arthur Allston.

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:32.580
He was a man of few words.

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:36.300
He never complained, no matter 
how dangerous the mission.

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:39.890
He was a silent man who 
always followed orders.

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:44.830
He rarely ever talked about what 
he wanted or would like to do.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:48.080
That's all I know.

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:53.830
I think the reason he keeps heading east is 
because there's something important there.

00:12:54.220 --> 00:12:57.460
Does anything come to mind?

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:04.020
Even if something did, there's no point.

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:08.360
I came here to kill him, not to help him.

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:12.600
But... he's been trying so 
hard not to harm anyone!

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:14.970
He still has his humanity!

00:13:15.550 --> 00:13:19.200
If he continues forward, he's going 
to destroy the iron bridge.

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:22.650
That bridge is supporting the 
peaceful age we live in now.

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:27.440
That peace is what we threw 
away our humanity to achieve.

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:35.070
We Incarnates, beings from the past, 
cannot be allowed to destroy it.

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:39.440
But he's not a being from the past...

00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:44.630
He's trying to make his wish come true, 
despite being so hurt!

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:46.970
How is he any different from us?!

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:51.710
He's also a person trying to 
live in this peaceful age!

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:57.680
He's not even allowed to dream?

00:13:57.680 --> 00:13:59.630
That's too tragic!

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.180
That should be all of them.

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:07.370
Good work.

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:14.520
What's the matter?

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:17.130
Is this about Behemoth?

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.120
Isn't there something we can do?

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:22.890
If you're asking if we can save him... No.

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:26.180
His body is just too big.

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:29.210
The danger he poses is 
something we can't risk.

00:14:29.210 --> 00:14:31.420
Even without the threat to the iron bridge,

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:34.390
we'd be ordered to eliminate 
him sooner or later.

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:42.030
The best we can do is make sure he 
doesn't suffer in his final moments.

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:44.040
That's all.

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:54.160
Let's get to work.

00:15:00.740 --> 00:15:03.190
I need to go talk to him one more time...

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:11.460
It can't be...

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:18.180
Blown to smithereens, 
just like the boss wanted.

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:37.350
What's going on?

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:39.700
Artie's on the move...

00:15:40.360 --> 00:15:41.420
Hank!

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:45.890
There's been a change of plans. 
We're going to take him down right here.

00:15:47.990 --> 00:15:49.900
Were you able to plant the explosives?

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:51.810
Just on the cliff, as we originally planned.

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:53.430
It's not enough to fill the valley.

00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:56.000
That means we have some 
leftover explosives, right?

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:58.060
Do you remember the point I told you about?

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:06.200
That's the signal.

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:20.340
<i>This won't be enough to completely stop him.</i>

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:22.320
<i>But now...</i>

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:31.450
<i>With no escape route, the explosion 
will be many times more effective.</i>

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:33.970
<i>Even you shouldn't be able to survive this...</i>

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:59.520
Please! Just stop!

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:04.900
Why do you keep going?

00:18:05.170 --> 00:18:08.490
Can't you understand what 
we're saying anymore?

00:18:08.490 --> 00:18:12.740
If you have any humanity left, please!

00:18:12.740 --> 00:18:13.870
Stop!

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:21.230
Artie!

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:27.840
Don't destroy the new age that we...
 that <i>you</i> created!

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:56.280
The ocean?

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:27.660
"I want to see the ocean..." 
That's what he told me.

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:35.970
I would love to see the ocean, 
even if it's just once.

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:40.390
Once the war is over, there will be peace.

00:19:40.390 --> 00:19:41.990
You can go see it then.

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:52.340
You had that part destroyed...

00:19:52.340 --> 00:19:55.100
so he could see the ocean from there.

00:19:56.870 --> 00:19:59.310
But I'm also the one who killed him.

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:01.760
That fact doesn't change.

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:14.130
Still, his wish came true...

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:16.360
All thanks to you, Hank.

00:22:03.220 --> 00:22:08.200
We just received a report. 
We've found out where he is.

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:10.930
Whitechurch, the City of Steam.

00:22:11.410 --> 00:22:14.420
There was a man there who 
matched his description.

00:22:17.090 --> 00:22:18.480
Who's she talking about?

00:22:18.900 --> 00:22:20.830
Cain Madhouse.

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:24.660
He's the former deputy captain 
of the Incarnate squad...

00:22:25.140 --> 00:22:30.250
and the one who unleashed the 
Incarnates upon this world!

00:22:40.220 --> 00:22:42.200
My, what a handsome man...

00:22:42.940 --> 00:22:45.070
Hey there.

00:22:45.070 --> 00:22:46.880
Want to have some fun with us?

00:22:49.820 --> 00:22:52.380
P-Please, not here...

00:22:55.330 --> 00:22:57.680
H-Hey! Are you all right?

00:23:07.530 --> 00:23:12.120
How boring... What value does 
a dull night like this have?

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:14.860
Absolutely none. Isn't that right?

00:23:15.180 --> 00:23:17.280
Yes, Master Cain!

00:23:25.380 --> 00:23:29.030
No one is just bad. They all...

00:23:29.030 --> 00:23:31.050
We have to do whatever it takes to survive.

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:32.850
Those claw marks...

00:23:32.850 --> 00:23:34.680
You're going to kill him, right?

00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:39.080
It's our job as Incarnates 
to eliminate those invaders!

00:23:36.930 --> 00:23:39.930
Gargoyle's Judgment
